# Acceptance record: round 2

**Conclusion: accepted.** The assembled delivery at game-developer `a2884c82ed6e1c98fb48361d45f482c0624b1ffc` + artist
`5565bd38fc502926f540b4d319079c4c85a71c56` (brief and assignment at producer `e24bb9b5f4e84d9bb76077ea23bf0a503251d53f`) is the game
the input asks for this round: classic Super Mario Bros. 1 as a web game, now World 1 and World 2 (2-1 to 2-4). It is played as one
continuous game from the title. It meets the brief's P0 (World 1 unchanged) and P1 (World 2 complete and faithful, reached from 1-4 and
from the 1-2 warp pipe). Its game files are identical to release `build-6` in `world/producer` (`build-6.zip`, sha256
3fb7eb078b063b8609d60faf2266fa787d8fe178bc201a563382ee8ca3005b2c). The only extra files in the delivery are the developer's `tests/`,
`tools/` and `.gitignore` (checked with `diff -rq` of `ht-role delivery` against the unzipped zip).

## What I inspected and played (producer, headless Chromium with Playwright, file://)
- The unzipped build-6 starts from `index.html` at `#level=1-1`, `2-1`, `2-2`, `2-3` and `2-4`. There are no page errors and no
  missing-asset warnings (`notes/shots/b6_grid.png`).
- Developer suites on the delivery: levels 28/28, world2 40/40, mechanics 20/20, mechanics2 26/26, mechanics3 19/19, sound_input 7/7.
- I swam through 2-2 by keyboard myself (`notes/shots/b6_2-2_swim.png`).
- I replayed the playtester's continuous key log myself on the unzipped zip
  (`playtests/build-6/evidence/campaign_w12/campaign_log.json`, real KeyboardEvents, Chromium stepped). It runs title -> 1-1 ... 1-4 ->
  2-1 ... 2-4 -> clear screen -> title in 19,414 logic frames, with 3 lives, 0 deaths, 127,150 points and 34 coins.
  - Its 67 game events (flags, pipes, springboard throw, axes, all-clear) and 640 sound calls are identical to the playtester's.
  - It has 0 page errors and 0 failed requests.
  - Screens checked by eye: `notes/shots/b6_cw12_w2.png` (2-2 water and exit pipe, flag, 2-3 bridge, 2-4 castle with Bowser over
    lava, "YOU CLEARED WORLD 2", title with the top score).

## What the checks found
- **qa** (`qa/reports/build-6.md`, qa `5dce9c3018636a45ed9c2177c89354434e9ebaf1`):
  - The World 1 gate passes: smoke check clean, 1-1 83/83, P2 43/43, lift trials 270/270, fair 1-1 bot.
  - World 2 `map_compare` shows 0 differences against the original decode for every 2-x area.
  - `check_w2` passes 111/111. It covers progression from 1-4 and the 1-2 warp, vine and coin heaven, the springboard, Paratroopas,
    Piranhas, swimming and the surface limit, Bloopers, Cheep Cheeps, the exit pipe, flying Cheep Cheeps, firebars, Podoboos, lifts,
    the fake Bowser turning into a Koopa, the axe, Toad, and the end screen returning to the title.
  - qa reports no defects.
- **playtester** (producer#14; `playtests/build-6/report.md` at playtester `6cdc7afa9a233b2fcddf7c4f7ef70634cc244b83`; videos in
  release `playtest-build-6`):
  - One continuous game from the title through World 1 and World 2 to the clear screen and title, with real keys, played three ways
    (Chromium stepped, Chromium real time, Firefox). Each gives the same events.
  - Score, coins and lives carry over from 1-4 into 2-1. The 1-2 warp pipe 2 leads to 2-1.
  - Every World 2 mechanic in the brief was probed and works.
  - World 1 shows no regression: the World 1 area pictures are pixel-identical to build-5's, and the result files are identical or
    differ only for explained reasons.
  - The playtester reports no blocker and no major defect.

## Findings left open, and why they do not block (decisions in `brief.md`, "Decisions on the build-6 playtest")
- F-1, the springboard and Podoboo make no sound: allowed by the brief's "as needed". A jump sound on the high throw is optional polish.
- F-2, water physics: the measured sink and the missing horizontal friction match SMB1. The brief's wording was corrected.
- F-3, 2-3 has no Koopas: the Koopa entries are hard-mode only in the original data, and qa's map comparison shows 0 differences.
- F-6, the Podoboo count, and F-7, where coin heaven drops Mario: both follow the original data.
- Optional polish, not blocking:
  - F-4: Mario can swim up into the HUD rows.
  - F-5: coin heaven has no music of its own and falls back to the overworld tune, as documented.
  - P-1: README and file headers name tools that are only in the source repositories.
  - P-3: small windows are clipped and there are no touch controls; the brief targets desktop keyboard.
- P2 continue (A + Start after game over) is not implemented. It is optional in the brief.
- Provenance: level layouts follow the original maps (tile layout and object positions only). All graphics and audio are original
  work by the artist position.
- **Not verified by anyone:**
  - sound by ear (checked only as decoded files and the game's sound calls);
  - human input latency;
  - a side-by-side comparison with the NES original beyond the decoded map data;
  - coin heaven coins collected in a full play (probed only).

# Acceptance record: round 1

**Conclusion: accepted.** The assembled delivery at game-developer `64cdad2a466e670275fbc0bf69b4c9afac1b99d8` + artist
`144b1149ff7aa4cd2bfbd8e88e3572183f399cdd` (assignment/brief at producer `8685f2d843f6c0c7c24152c334a77f9786f5b552` and later,
unchanged) is the game the input asks for: *复刻经典版本的超级马里奥 1，做成网页游戏*, recreating classic Super Mario Bros. 1 as a
web game. It meets the brief's P1 bar (World 1-1 complete and faithful) and P2 (World 1-2 to 1-4 playable to the end). P3 (later
worlds) is not part of this round, as the brief settles. This is the same content as release `build-5` in `world/producer`
(`build-5.zip`, sha256 f4ce1ab2fe7021ffa7a83481d6cd23b699325494bbc0a496c65ee309f2d1404c).

## What I inspected and played (producer, headless Chromium 1280 with Playwright, file://)
- The assembled delivery (`ht-role delivery`) and the unzipped build-5 zip both start from `index.html` with no server, no network,
  no page errors and no missing-asset warnings.
- Developer suites on the delivery: levels 27/27, sound_input 7/7, mechanics 20/20, mechanics2 26/26, mechanics3 19/19.
- The scripted bot plays 1-1 from the title to the flag with 0 deaths and goes into 1-2.
- I ran 1-1 by keyboard input from the title (run with B, jump with A).
- Screens checked by eye (`notes/shots/b5_grid.png`): title, 1-1, the 1-2 warp zone, the 1-3 start, Bowser on the 1-4 bridge, and
  Toad's "THANK YOU MARIO!". They read as SMB1: NES palette, 256×240, crisp integer scaling, the original HUD.
- Earlier builds: build-1 to build-4 (`notes/builds.md`).

## What the checks found
- **qa** (`qa/reports/build-5.md`, qa `4edc98dcba66956319b0517b3bc9faa2f0cc7fd8`):
  - 1-1 83/83 and P2 43/43; the smoke check is clean; qa's fair bot clears 1-1.
  - All 9 lifts pass the multi-phase landing trials. The same trials fail on build-4, so they reproduce and confirm the N4 fix.
  - game-developer#7, #8, #9 and #11 stay fixed, and the `#level` fallback works.
  - qa has no open defects and passes build-5.
- **playtester** (producer#12; `playtests/build-5/report.md` at playtester `f4c1b1ee25f77ec5fb273473da41cd2cf012d202`; videos in release
  `playtest-build-5`):
  - Two continuous games from the title through 1-1…1-4 to Toad and the clear screen, with real key events, each replayed in
    Chromium stepped, Chromium real time and Firefox with identical end states. One run rides the rising 1-3 lift.
  - All 29 P1 rows pass, and every P2 row passes.
  - No softlocks or fall-throughs, 0 page errors and 0 failed requests.
  - N4 (the 1-3 lift), N5 (enemy facing), N6a and N7 are verified fixed, with no regressions against build-3.
  - The playtester reports no blocker, major or minor defect.

## Findings left open, and why they do not block
- README and file headers in the zip mention developer tools that live only in the source repositories. This is polish with no
  effect on play; it is noted to the owners as optional.
- Small windows are clipped and there are no touch controls. The brief makes desktop keyboard the target this round.
- The multi-coin brick pays 13 coins, with no reference to check against. There are no Podoboos in 1-4: the decoded 1-4 Podoboo
  entries are hard-mode only.
- Warp pipes end on a "worlds 2-8 not in this version" screen, as the World 1 scope intends.
- **Provenance** (producer decision): level layouts follow the original maps (tile layout only), as the brief's "layout of 1-1 as
  in the original" requires. All graphics and audio are original work by the artist position, with no ROM graphics, recorded
  Nintendo audio or game code. The decoder that ported the original parser was removed from the delivery (game-developer#12).
- **Not verified by anyone:** sound by ear (no audio device in any sandbox; audio was checked as decoded, non-silent files and as
  the game's sound calls), human input latency, and a side-by-side comparison with the NES original.
